  "findings": [
    "ComponentRoseGroupingHeader preferred height includes padded getTextHeight plus max(commentHeight-15,0); the literal15 is directly cited. SheetBlock1 contributes padding around nonempty blocks. The new note/group scheduling uses those contributions and the prior padding3/7 cases recover.",
    "All eight fresh multiline/empty-else/attached-note/padding controls fail. The simplest legacy primary case differs only at the reply label x by1px (153.3333 Java versus152.3333 Rust with padding1), growing to6px at padding6. This shows the component-padding dependency is not coherent across scheduling and ordinary-message text origins. Attached self notes remain6px too low at padding3, and the note+delay combination is4px too short at padding2.",
    "The code retains multiple calculations of note_top/preferred height and special self-note scheduling rather than deriving ArrowAndNoteBox vertical centering from max(arrowHeight,noteHeight). These are traced to Java ArrowAndNoteBox constructor/getPreferredHeight and Step1Abstract#createNoteBox. Do not repair by adding offsets to these fixtures; unify the component measurement data flow.",
    "All14 accounts were present byte-for-byte in earlier chronological commits before their corresponding code. See provenance.json and commit-mapping.json. Main release tiers remain11181/11251 product-library and10497/11251 assisted-library; source-only CLI cohort403/955 with10 invalid references; no regressions observed.",
    "Verdict applies to whole source-to-SVG recovery with the dependencies described above. Positive component-local observations are explicitly bounded and are not acceptance. Every mismatch and negative remains in the standing suite."
